(7186144, 1103970, 100393, '<td valign="top">his image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. How it has a slightly 70s feel - I don''t know how you''ve pulled that off.<br/>2. The near-merger of her legs with the chair.<br/>3. The utterly precise conversion - perfectly toned.<br/>4. How spartan the room is - we are left to guess its function - like a hotel room, but not quite.<br/>5. The perfect exposure - this sort of window as backlight is tricky - I like how we can discern the inside and the outside.<br/>6. The reflection in the table.<br/> <br/>This is a grower. Bumped from 8 to 9 as I formed the comment.</td>', 'his image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. How it has a slightly 70s feel - I don''t know how you''ve pulled that off.2. The near-merger of her legs with the chair.3. The utterly precise conversion - perfectly toned.4. How spartan the room is - we are left to guess its function - like a hotel room, but not quite.5. The perfect exposure - this sort of window as backlight is tricky - I like how we can discern the inside and the outside.6. The reflection in the table. This is a grower. Bumped from 8 to 9 as I formed the comment.', '2014-03-06 10:44:39.000000', NULL, 1),
